From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:39:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08031/11362] The A/A floor that certified the correction was
 measured at the wrong configuration

The operator asked to finish 4 missing pre-flight cells and check the context truncation. The
context hypothesis is FALSIFIED -- every arm ran at n_ctx=32768, symmetric, read from /props per
cell and from the live server argv, with zero occurrences of any overflow mode and the detector
verified live on BOTH arms. The 16384 log that motivated it is from 2026-07-27 and had MTP on.
The 4 cells were never launched: the driver's global wall expired at +11672s against an 11520s cap.

The real problem was an ASSET confound. The base arm ran from a git worktree and the head arm from
the canonical checkout; two gitignored assets are not materialised by `git worktree add`, so the
base arm's load_live_action_effect_scorer() returned None, no ActionEffectExpansionPrior was built,
and the search frontier expanded in a different order. Neither A/A floor could catch it -- head and
headb both ran from the canonical repo, base and baseb both from the worktree, so both floors held
the asset axis fixed by construction. That is why 10/10 replicate pairs were IDENTICAL while every
A/B perturbed.

Then the correction repeated the mistake one level up, and that is what this commit is really
about. The A/A run to certify the deconfounded result launched after the symlinks had been removed
again (both dirs carry an ns-identical mtime -- one unlink batch), so it replicated the NO-ASSET
configuration while certifying a WITH-ASSET A/B. It matched the old arm byte for byte and was read
as "vc33 fails its own noise floor", retracting the one surviving cell. Re-measured properly --
assets restored and verified LOADED, not merely present -- the vc33 A/A is IDENTICAL across three
replicates while the A/B still differs at index 17. vc33 is certified. The prior artifact's
0-attributable and p=1.0 are withdrawn; p=1.0 asserted no discordant pair could exist.

Neither error is visible in the traces, the commit shas, or any completeness flag, so the fix makes
configuration something the analysis CHECKS. classify_trace_pair takes a_config/b_config, and
preflight_verdict refuses a floor whose configuration does not match the comparison it certifies:
AA_FLOOR_IS_NOT_AN_AA when the replicate's own arms differ, AA_FLOOR_CONFIG_MISMATCH when it
matches neither arm under test. Legacy callers are unchanged but the verdict now reports which
cells went unverified, because reading "nobody said" as "checked and matched" is how this happened.

Outcome: 1 certified attributable of 4 deconfounded cells, 3 observed nulls, zero missing (the two
truncated cells were re-run at head's identical in-cell wall and both completed). The ceiling is
p=0.125 even if all 4 had been discordant, against the 6 pairs alpha=0.05 needs, and 8 grid cells
still have a confounded base arm. INCONCLUSIVE -- not a refusal, and not evidence the span is inert.

Also withdrawn: the claim that the assets made cells slower. basefix2/tr87 finished in 932s at the
same configuration where the earlier run was killed at 1500s -- faster than head's own 1064s. It
was machine load, unrecorded, so missingness was non-random with respect to when a cell ran.

Banked ARC levels remain 3/3 and the submission gate is NOT met; nothing here measured a score.

